# ------------------------------------------------------------- in-string

[break] in-string-searches-the-code
rule: An `in-string` text is looked for only inside string literals, never in code or comments.
file: xtask/src/mutate/lex.rs
in: strings_matching
find: let Some(content) = string_content(literal) else {
replace: let Some(content) = Some(0..literal.len()) else {
caught-by:
    mutate::lex::tests::a_text_is_found_only_inside_the_string_literals

[break] in-string-takes-the-first-of-several
rule: An `in-string` text that is in two places is refused, and `occurrence` says which is meant.
file: xtask/src/mutate/lex.rs
in: locate_in_strings
find: (several, None) => Err(Missing::Ambiguous(
replace:
    (several, None) => Ok((several[0].clone(), scopes)),
    (several, None) => Err(Missing::Ambiguous(
caught-by:
    mutate::lex::tests::a_text_is_found_only_inside_the_string_literals

[break] in-string-counts-an-occurrence-from-nought
rule: `occurrence` is counted from 1, across the string literals in source order.
file: xtask/src/mutate/lex.rs
in: locate_in_strings
find: asked.checked_sub(1)
replace: asked.checked_sub(0)
caught-by:
    mutate::lex::tests::a_text_is_found_only_inside_the_string_literals

[break] in-string-reads-an-escaped-quote-as-the-end
rule: A backslash escapes the character after it, so `\"` does not end a string literal.
file: xtask/src/mutate/lex.rs
in: string_content
find: b'\\' => at += 2,
replace: b'\\' => at += 1,
caught-by:
    mutate::lex::tests::the_text_of_a_string_literal_is_what_is_between_its_quotes

[break] in-string-takes-a-literal-with-anything-after-it
rule: A string literal's text ends at its closing quote, which must be the last byte of the token.
file: xtask/src/mutate/lex.rs
in: string_content
find: (end + 1 + hashes == literal.len()).then_some(start..end)
replace: Some(start..end)
caught-by:
    mutate::lex::tests::the_text_of_a_string_literal_is_what_is_between_its_quotes

[break] in-string-allows-a-replacement-that-is-not-one-string
rule: A break's `replace` must leave the literal one string: a quote that no backslash escapes would end it.
file: xtask/src/mutate/mod.rs
in: locate
find: && !is_one_string(&text)
replace: && false
caught-by:
    mutate::tests::an_in_string_that_would_not_leave_one_string_or_change_nothing_is_refused

[break] in-string-allows-a-change-that-is-none
rule: A break whose `replace` is the text it replaces changes nothing, and is refused.
file: xtask/src/mutate/mod.rs
in: locate
find: if source[range.clone()] == one.replace {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    mutate::tests::an_in_string_that_would_not_leave_one_string_or_change_nothing_is_refused

[break] in-string-is-compared-as-the-word-and-not-the-literal
rule: Two breaks that make the same change are refused whichever key made it: an `in-string` is compared as the literal it changes.
file: xtask/src/mutate/mod.rs
in: check
find: Some((literal, text)) => change_of(source, code, &literal, &text),
replace: Some(_) => change_of(source, code, &range, &one.replace),
caught-by:
    mutate::tests::an_in_string_that_makes_the_change_of_another_break_is_refused_as_a_copy

[break] in-string-ends-in-a-comma-that-is-the-formatters
rule: A comma at the end of an `in-string` is text, not a comma that `rustfmt` moves.
file: xtask/src/mutate/mod.rs
in: preflight
find: if !one.in_string && ends_in_a_layout_comma(&one.find) {
replace: if ends_in_a_layout_comma(&one.find) {
caught-by:
    mutate::tests::a_comma_at_the_end_of_an_in_string_is_text_and_not_a_layout_comma

[break] in-string-and-find-are-allowed-together
rule: A break has a `find` or an `in-string`, not both.
